## Configuring Turborepo Task Graph Pipelines & Caching Rules

Turborepo uses DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph) task definitions in `turbo.json` to execute tasks in optimal topological order. Unchanged build outputs are restored instantly from local or remote build caches.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  "pipeline": {
    "build": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "outputs": ["dist/**", ".next/**"]
    },
    "lint": {
      "outputs": []
    },
    "dev": {
      "cache": false,
      "persistent": true
    }
  }
}
```

---

## Accelerating Builds with Bun & Workspace Protocol

Leveraging Bun as the package installer and script executor cuts package installation times down to sub-seconds while offering native TypeScript execution without transpilation steps.

---

## CI/CD Optimization: Incremental Builds & Remote Caching setup

Connecting Turborepo to remote cache storage ensures CI runners bypass building untouched apps, cutting deployment build pipeline durations by over 70%.

---

## Developer Experience: Monorepo Scripts & Automated Versioning

Utilizing Changesets simplifies versioning and changelog generation across monorepo workspace packages prior to deployment releases.
